@node LibreClaw API Reference
@section DEFUN Reference

All DEFUNs listed here are Emacs C primitives and are only available
when cmacs is built with @code{--with-cmacs-libreclaw}.

@subsection Lifecycle

@table @code
@item cmacs-libreclaw-start
Elisp wrapper.  Ensures @code{cmacs-libreclaw-config-file} is set,
starts cmacs-podomation if needed, calls
@code{cmacs-libreclaw--start-internal}, and loads the GI typelib.

@item cmacs-libreclaw--start-internal
C DEFUN.  Create the @code{LcApp} and register the podomation bridge
module on the shared engine.  Signals @code{cmacs-libreclaw-error}
if the config file is unset, podomation is not running, or
libreclaw fails to start.

@item cmacs-libreclaw-stop
Disconnect signal handlers, stop the embedded LcApp, deactivate
the bridge module.

@item cmacs-libreclaw-running-p
Return @code{t} if the LcApp is live.

@item cmacs-libreclaw-set-config-file FILE
Store @var{FILE} as the YAML path for the next start.

@item cmacs-libreclaw-get-config-file
Return the currently configured YAML path, or @code{nil}.

@item cmacs-libreclaw-reload-config
Re-read the YAML file and re-emit libreclaw's @code{config-reloaded}
signal.  Use this for live edits to the @emph{same} file; for
switching to a @emph{different} file, use
@code{cmacs-libreclaw-load-config} below.

@item cmacs-libreclaw-load-config FILE &optional RESTART
Elisp autoload.  One-command config switcher.  Expands
@var{FILE}, asserts it's readable, sets
@code{cmacs-libreclaw-config-file}, and --- if libreclaw is
already running --- cleanly stops and restarts the subsystem
against the new path when @var{RESTART} is non-nil.  When
libreclaw is not running, stages the path for the next
@code{cmacs-libreclaw-start} call.  Interactive:
@kbd{M-x cmacs-libreclaw-load-config} prompts for the YAML path
with completion.

@item cmacs-libreclaw-version
Return libreclaw's version as a @samp{N.N.N} string.

@item cmacs-libreclaw-podomation-shared-p
Return @code{t} if the bridge module is registered on cmacs's
shared PodEngine.
@end table

@subsection Config

@table @code
@item cmacs-libreclaw-config-validate FILE
Parse @var{FILE} without starting an LcApp.  Signals
@code{cmacs-libreclaw-error} on parse failure.

@item cmacs-libreclaw-config-preview FILE
Return a plist summarising @var{FILE}'s contents.

@item cmacs-libreclaw-generate-default-config &optional WS AI OVERWRITE
Elisp.  Write a minimal default YAML to
@file{WS/config.yaml} (defaulting to
@code{cmacs-libreclaw-default-workspace}).  Uses libreclaw's
@code{lc_hatch_*} API, so the schema tracks whatever libreclaw
version is linked.  Sets @code{cmacs-libreclaw-config-file} to
the written path and returns it.

@item cmacs-libreclaw-ensure-config
Elisp.  Called by @code{cmacs-libreclaw-start}.  Adopts any
existing default config or (with user consent) auto-generates
one via @code{cmacs-libreclaw-generate-default-config}.
@end table

@subsection Cmacs channel

@table @code
@item cmacs-libreclaw-open &optional DIRECTORY
Elisp (autoload).  Primary user entry point.  Creates or
switches to a libreclaw chat buffer for the project containing
@var{DIRECTORY} (defaults to the current @code{default-directory}).
Starts libreclaw and generates a default config if needed.  Each
project gets its own buffer with its own persistent AI session.

@item cmacs-libreclaw-cmacs-channel-available-p
C DEFUN.  Returns @code{t} if the in-process LcCmacsChannel is
bound.  Requires both @code{(cmacs-libreclaw-running-p)} and
@code{channels: cmacs: enabled: true} in the loaded YAML.

@item cmacs-libreclaw-cmacs-channel-inject ROOM-ID SENDER-ID BODY &optional SENDER-NAME
C DEFUN.  Pushes @var{BODY} as an inbound message on
@var{ROOM-ID} into libreclaw's pipeline.  Routes through
@code{LcChannelManager}, @code{LcRouter}, and
@code{LcSessionManager}, so the AI provider generates a response
that eventually arrives through
@code{cmacs-libreclaw--on-cmacs-response}.

@item cmacs-libreclaw-cmacs-channel-register-room ROOM-ID
C DEFUN.  Marks @var{ROOM-ID} as a known room.  Idempotent.

@item cmacs-libreclaw-cmacs-channel-unregister-room ROOM-ID
C DEFUN.  Drops @var{ROOM-ID} from the known-rooms set.

@item cmacs-libreclaw-cmacs-channel-list-rooms
C DEFUN.  Returns the list of known room identifiers.

@item cmacs-libreclaw-cmacs-channel-has-room-p ROOM-ID
C DEFUN.  Returns non-nil if @var{ROOM-ID} is registered.

@item cmacs-libreclaw-cmacs-channel-save-history
Elisp.  Persists the current buffer's history region to
@file{<history-dir>/<sha>.org}.  Called automatically on
@code{after-save-hook} and @code{kill-buffer-hook}; bound to
@kbd{C-c C-s} interactively.

@item cmacs-libreclaw-hatch-add-cmacs HANDLE
C DEFUN.  Appends a cmacs (in-process) channel to the hatch
context.  No parameters.
@end table

@subsection Channels

@table @code
@item cmacs-libreclaw-list-channels
@code{((id . kind) @dots{})} of active channels.

@item cmacs-libreclaw-channel-kind ID
Kind symbol for @var{ID}.

@item cmacs-libreclaw-channel-connected-p ID
@code{t} if connected.

@item cmacs-libreclaw-channel-connect ID
Async connect.

@item cmacs-libreclaw-channel-disconnect ID
Async disconnect.
@end table

@subsection Messaging

@table @code
@item cmacs-libreclaw-send-message CHANNEL-ID ROOM-ID BODY &optional HTML-BODY THREAD-ID
Queue an outbound message.  Returns @code{t} immediately; delivery
is async.

@item cmacs-libreclaw-join-room CHANNEL-ID ROOM-ID
Signals @code{cmacs-libreclaw-error} — libreclaw 0.18.0 does not
expose a public join-room API.  Use @code{auto_join} in config.yaml.

@item cmacs-libreclaw-leave-room CHANNEL-ID ROOM-ID
Same — not supported in 0.18.0.
@end table

@subsection Hatch

@table @code
@item cmacs-libreclaw-hatch-new WORKSPACE-DIR
Create a new hatch context.  Returns an integer handle.

@item cmacs-libreclaw-hatch-free HANDLE
Release the hatch context.

@item cmacs-libreclaw-hatch-set-name HANDLE NAME
@item cmacs-libreclaw-hatch-set-identity HANDLE PATH
@item cmacs-libreclaw-hatch-set-ai HANDLE KIND
@item cmacs-libreclaw-hatch-add-matrix HANDLE HS USER-ID TOKEN
@item cmacs-libreclaw-hatch-add-local HANDLE &optional PROMPT
@item cmacs-libreclaw-hatch-add-email HANDLE IMAP SMTP USER PASS
@item cmacs-libreclaw-hatch-add-webhook HANDLE PORT PATH-PREFIX
@item cmacs-libreclaw-hatch-enable-podomation HANDLE &optional DSL
@item cmacs-libreclaw-hatch-enable-audit HANDLE &optional DB-PATH
@item cmacs-libreclaw-hatch-preview HANDLE
@item cmacs-libreclaw-hatch-finalize HANDLE &optional OVERWRITE
See the Hatch Wizard chapter for the full wizard flow.
@end table
